### Thousand Faces, One Mistake - Setup, Borrowed-Role
Prerequisite: You Meng’s Borrowed Robes, CL 10+
When you use Set the Scene, create one visible role:
cringing coward;
arrogant noble;
loyal servant;
wounded traveler;
drunken performer;
officious inspector;
familiar rival;
another role approved by the GM.
Until Set the Scene ends:
gain Advantage on one Charisma (Deception) or Charisma (Performance) check consistent with the role;
if the Foil fulfills your Proposition, choose to become Invisible to the Foil until the end of the current turn after your Punchline resolves.
Invisible from this talent ends early if you make an attack roll or deal damage.
The role does not automatically deceive creatures that cannot perceive the performance.

#### Soul-in-the-Body Treatment - Purification, Spirit
You can treat injuries where the body and spirit have begun to disagree.
When you use Purify the Pulse on a target, you may spend 2 additional CP to affect one of the following:
possession;
forced soul displacement;
an effect preventing the soul from controlling the body;
an effect trapping the target’s awareness outside its body;
a Spirit Awakening effect causing Stunned, Unconscious, Frightened, or Charmed.
The target immediately makes a new saving throw against the effect with Advantage.
If the effect does not normally allow a saving throw, make a Cultivation Check against the effect’s save DC. On a success, the effect is suppressed for 1 minute.
This talent does not destroy the possessing entity or spiritual prison unless another feature says otherwise.
